jobs.description:
The Chief Marketing Officer (CMO) is responsible for developing and leading the company’s overall marketing strategy, overseeing brand management, market promotion, digital marketing, customer acquisition, market research, and marketing performance management. As a key member of the senior executive team, the CMO translates corporate business objectives into actionable market growth plans. By optimizing the allocation of marketing resources, enhancing brand influence, and expanding the customer base, the CMO drives revenue growth, increases market share, and fosters long-term brand value.

Core Responsibilities

I. Corporate Marketing Strategy
- Develop the overall corporate marketing strategy and long-term market development plans.
- Define marketing direction, market priorities, and growth targets based on corporate business objectives.
- Identify emerging market opportunities and potential customer segments.
- Establish mechanisms for the execution of marketing strategies and the evaluation of performance.
- Ensure that all marketing activities are aligned with the company’s broader business strategy.

II. Brand Management and Market Positioning
- Oversee corporate brand strategy, market positioning, and the development of brand identity.
- Establish a brand value framework and standards for market communication.
- Supervise brand promotion, corporate communications, and public relations (PR) activities.
- Drive improvements in brand awareness, market influence, and customer loyalty.
- Manage brand assets and foster the growth of long-term brand value.

III. Market Promotion and Customer Acquisition
- Lead integrated marketing and multi-channel promotional campaigns.
- Formulate strategies for customer acquisition, lead generation, and market expansion.
- Optimize both online and offline marketing channels and promotional resources.
- Foster synergy between marketing initiatives and the sales team to increase customer conversion rates.
- Evaluate the effectiveness of promotional activities and continuously refine customer acquisition strategies.

IV. Digital Marketing and Marketing Innovation
- Develop strategies for digital marketing and online business promotion.
- Oversee SEO, SEM, social media, content marketing, and email marketing.
- Drive the adoption of marketing automation, data analytics, and AI-powered tools.
- Assess the return on investment (ROI) across digital marketing channels.
- Explore innovative marketing models and new opportunities for market promotion.

V. Market Research and Competitive Analysis
- Monitor industry trends, market demand, and the competitive landscape;
- Research target customer behavior, consumption preferences, and market shifts;
- Evaluate competitors’ market strategies and brand performance;
- Identify market growth opportunities and potential business risks;
- Translate market research findings into actionable marketing decisions and business development recommendations.

VI. Marketing Performance and Budget Management
- Establish an enterprise-level marketing performance management and KPI evaluation framework;
- Develop marketing budgets and oversee resource allocation;
- Monitor customer acquisition costs (CAC), return on marketing investment (ROMI), and conversion performance;
- Periodically evaluate the outcomes of marketing initiatives and devise optimization strategies;
- Report marketing performance to the CEO, the Board of Directors, and senior management.

VII. Team Building and Cross-Functional Collaboration
- Build and lead the corporate marketing management team;
- Manage senior-level personnel, such as the VP of Marketing, Marketing Directors, and Brand Directors;
- Collaborate with Sales, Product, Customer Success, and Corporate Communications departments;
- Develop plans for marketing talent cultivation, performance evaluation, and organizational development;
- Foster a marketing culture centered on market growth, customer value, and business outcomes.

Qualifications

Education
- Bachelor’s degree or higher in Marketing, Business Administration, Management, Communications, or a related field;
- MBA, EMBA, or a Master’s degree in Marketing Strategy is preferred;
- Professional training in digital marketing, brand management, or business strategy is a plus.

Work Experience
- 20+ years of experience in marketing, brand management, or business growth;
- 15+ years of experience in senior marketing management and team leadership;
- Prior experience in executive-level roles—such as Chief Marketing Officer (CMO), SVP of Marketing, or VP of Marketing—is preferred;
- Proven experience in developing enterprise-level marketing strategies, building brands, and driving market expansion;
- A successful track record of managing large marketing budgets, leading cross-regional marketing teams, and executing multi-channel promotional campaigns.

Core Competencies
- Marketing Strategy & Development;
- Brand Management;
- Digital Marketing;
- Market Research & Competitive Analysis;
- Customer Acquisition & Retention;
- Demand Generation;
- Marketing Performance Analytics;
- Marketing Budget Management;
- Revenue Growth Strategy;
- Integrated Marketing Communications;
- Cross-Functional Leadership;
- Executive Strategic Planning.

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
- Achievement rate of corporate marketing strategic goals;
- Growth rate of brand awareness and market influence;
- Customer acquisition volume and conversion rates;
- Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC);
- Marketing Return on Investment (Marketing ROI);
- Market share growth rate;
- Revenue contribution by marketing channel;
- Customer retention rate and Customer Lifetime Value (CLV);
- Marketing project completion rate;
